  "details": "i moderate group publics a lot, usually in trending quest compatible not age verified instances, which attract a lot of bad actors. \n\nsometimes, we need to get someone out of the instance for different reasons. \n\nfor example:\n\n- if a user is asleep at the end of one of naku's acoustic sessions, we kick them from the instance because after the stream, instances are un-moderated. i would love to be able to kick a user but it not effect their trust rank, and if they wake up, they can join back. no cooldown.  \n\n- if a user is being a nuisance before the session, but we'd like for them to have access to the session which starts in 30 minutes, i'd like to be able to kick them for only 30 minutes and then they're more than welcome to come back. \n\ni think also being able to kick a user for the span of the event that the instance is linked to, so they're able to join the next one. \n\nadding a reason to the kick/ban/warn logs would be helpful too. with a moderation team of over 50 people, not everyone is able to communicate with each other as to why someone got kicked and which rule they broke.",
